    "text": "Let a vertical tower <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> of height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></math> stands on a horizontal ground. Let from a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> on the ground a man can see upto height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> of the tower with an angle of elevation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math>. When from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, he moves a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> in the direction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>, he can see the top <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of the tower with an angle of elevation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mi>h</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
