  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given a vertical tower <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> of height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></math> stands on a horizontal ground and from a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> on the ground a man can see upto height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> of the tower with an angle of elevation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&alpha;</mi></math>. When from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, he moves a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> in the direction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&rarr;</mo></mover></math>, he can see the top <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of the tower with an angle of elevation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&alpha;</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mi>h</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&alpha;</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to</p><p>Now on plotting the value in diagram we have,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0005_3e91b04226cd.png\" style=\"width: 315px; height: 250px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>Now in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>△</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>△</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn><mi>h</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>cot</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>from&nbsp;equation&nbsp;</mtext><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&alpha;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>tan</mi><mi>&alpha;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Now put&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;on simplifying we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mi>t</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>&alpha;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
